    "extraction": {
      "figure": "Figure 2",
      "caption": "Figure 2 : CARE architecture and training pipeline. (a) CARE framework with iBOT-style self-supervised pretraining using a teacher–student setup. CARE comprises three modules: the Adaptive Region Generator (ARG), adaptive region self-attention (ARSA), and Semantic and Prior Fusion (SPF). ARG partitions WSIs into morphologically coherent regions. ARSA operates within each adaptive region to derive region level features. SPF aggregates these features into a WSI embedding. (b) Cross-modal pretraining pipeline. RNA and protein encoders produce molecular embeddings, which are aligned to CARE’s WSI embedding via an InfoNCE loss.",
