      "id": "cvpr26-deaf8ceabab0",
      "figure": "Figure 2",
      "caption": "Figure 2. PhyOceanCast architecture overview. The model predicts ocean state evolution through residual learning with second order Markov roll-out strategy (top-left) and iterative diffusion refinement (top-right). Given previous states Xt−1 and Xt−2 as conditions with Time Encoder providing intra-annual temporal positioning, these inputs are fed into SGAN-MOC and PWTC modules: SGAN-MOC preserves spherical topology while enabling physics-aware cross-variable interactions, and PWTC enables depth-coupled variable interactions while decomposing ocean dynamics across multiple temporal scales with advection-diffusion constraints. The pipeline generates residual rt through reverse denoising, producing future ocean state Xt.",
      "page": 4,
      "captionRect": [
