      "id": "cvpr26-f34e1c16e7c5",
      "figure": "Figure 1",
      "caption": "Figure 1. Overview of F2Net’s multi-branch design. An adaptive frequency decomposition module splits the input into high- and low- frequency components. The high-frequency branch preserves details, while the low-frequency branch (with downsampling) includes short- and long-range sub-branches. A hybrid-frequency fusion (HFF) module integrates all features. Two auxiliary losses—Cross-Frequency Alignment Loss (CFAL) and Cross-Frequency Balance Loss (CFBL)—promote semantic consistency and balanced optimization.",
