  {
    "id": "cvpr26-9eccaa5463a2",
    "extraction": {
      "id": "cvpr26-9eccaa5463a2",
      "figure": "Figure 2",
      "caption": "Figure 2. Overview of PG-SFD. (a) PG-SFD consists of a pre-trained encoder, a feature adapter, and a decoder with multi-heads. Specif- ically, the features within the red dashed box are designated for the UAD task, while those in the green dashed box are dedicated for the anomaly classification task. (b) Presents the performance comparison of PG-SFD utilizing different visual backbones on the MVTec AD dataset[2, 13, 26, 27, 30, 33, 34, 38]. The results show that the model achieves optimal performance when using DINOv2 as the backbone network. (c) Illustrates the detailed structure of the Prototype Attention mechanism. (d) Presents the model details of the DPRM. In this module, the Normal Prototypes are injected into the classification branch as representations of normal features. They are then used in a differential calculation with Anomaly Prototypes to jointly optimize the entire model, effectively enlarging the inter-class margin.",
      "page": 4,
