      "figure": "Figure 3",
      "caption": "Figure 3. Overview of our method. Our pipeline is built around a MLP that serves as the inverse solver. Given the scattered field measurements Es from all transmitters and receivers, along with a spatial query x, the MLP directly predicts the relative permittivity ˆϵr(x). To enhance spatial expressiveness, we apply positional encoding γ(x) to the query position. During training, dashed lines indicate the supervision signals applied.",
