  {
    "id": "cvpr26-234c2237c5fa",
    "extraction": {
      "figure": "Figure 2",
      "caption": "Figure 2 : System Overview. We propose the first unified 3D Gaussian-based world model framework that simultaneously supports both scene understanding and scene generation.\nWe first employ a scene encoder to align the language information with the 3D Gaussians,\nresulting in language-augmented 3D Gaussian representations.\nThen, a designed Gaussian projector aligns the 3D Gaussian tokens,\n2D image tokens, and text tokens into a unified latent space.\nSubsequently, a task-aware hybrid sampling strategy is applied\nto select the most relevant 3D Gaussian tokens for the current query,\nwhich are then fed into the LLM.\nThe LLM produces both textual answers and high-level language features\nthat encapsulate world knowledge, which are later used\nto guide multi-modal scene generation.",
      "image_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2512.23180v3/GaussianDWM.png",
      "figureAnchor": "S2.F2",
      "panelIndex": 0,
      "panelCount": 1,
      "score": 33,
      "scoreReasons": [
