  {
    "id": "cvpr26-e023b87103b6",
    "extraction": {
      "id": "cvpr26-e023b87103b6",
      "figure": "Figure 3",
      "caption": "Figure 3. End-to-end example of the proposed HUMORCHAIN framework. Given an input image, HUMORCHAIN ﬁrst performs visual entity recognition and determines that the scene contains a person. It then evaluates whether the image exhibits humorous characteristics, concluding that it is not humorous. Next, the system assesses the plausibility of the scene and judges it as implausible. Based on this judg- ment, HUMORCHAIN activates the Absurdity reasoning pathway, guided by Incongruity–Resolution Theory, to generate a corresponding humorous caption that aligns with this type of humor. The red arrow indicates the path through which the caption is generated, while the black dashed arrows represent other possibilities.",
      "page": 5,
      "captionRect": [
