    "extraction": {
      "figure": "Figure 2",
      "caption": "Figure 2 : Illustration of our frequency-decoupled (DeCo) framework. In (a), traditional baseline models rely on a single DiT to jointly model both low-frequency semantics and high-frequency signals. (b) shows our DeCo framework, where a lightweight pixel decoder focuses on the high-frequency reconstruction, and the DiT models low-frequency semantics. As shown in (c), decoupling DiT from modeling high-frequency signals leads to better low-frequency semantic features in DiT Output, and higher image quality.",
      "image_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2511.19365v2/intro.png",
      "figureAnchor": "S1.F2",
      "panelIndex": 0,
