  {
    "id": "cvpr26-67779b0743cd",
    "extraction": {
      "figure": "Figure 2",
      "caption": "Figure 2 : Overview of our RiskProp framework. The encoder-only model takes a snippet of consecutive frames and predicts the current frame’s risk score.\nTo train such a model without “anomaly onset” labels and with only the objective collision frame label, two losses are proposed:\nThe Future-Frame Regularization Loss uses the next-frame’s detached prediction as a self-supervised target for high-risk signals backward propagation, while the Adaptive Monotonic Constraint Loss imposes a monotonicity constraint to ensure a non-decreasing overall risk trend. And we adopt the Binary Cross-Entropy loss to provide explicit supervision only at the collision frame. This enables stable, physically plausible risk curves without manual onset annotations.",
      "image_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2603.27165v1/framework.png",
      "figureAnchor": "S2.F2",
      "panelIndex": 0,
      "panelCount": 1,
