      "id": "cvpr26-c32ea0a1f107",
      "figure": "Figure 2",
      "caption": "Figure 2. Overview of the Proposed PGBL Framework. (a) Multi-Prototype Compact Constraint (MPCC): employs a frozen feature extractor and a trainable projection head to map features into a structured embedding space, organizing them into compact clusters via a dual-level prototype system optimized by multi-level contrastive loss; (b) Boundary-Aware Anomaly Synthesis (BAAS): performs cluster- based and boundary-aware anomaly synthesis. It first executes boundary identification, followed by adaptive Gaussian sampling and prototype-aware quality filtering to generate pseudo-anomalies; (c) Discriminative Boundary Refiner (DBR): a discriminator trained to distinguish normal features from pseudo-anomalies.",
      "page": 3,
