    "extraction": {
      "id": "cvpr26-e9728a39a150",
      "figure": "Figure 2",
      "caption": "Figure 2. Overview of our proposed HypoDepth. The network architecture comprises three main components: 1) Backbone: The image and event backbones respectively extract multi-resolution contextual features from image frames and event streams. 2) EIFusion. The fusion module adaptively fuses information from both modalities across multiple resolutions to produce unified contextual representations. 3) Depth Decoder. This decoder constructs a Depth Hypothesis Volume (DHV) and computes a 3D cost volume between DHV and the fused contextual features for lookup and geometry encoding. Subsequently, a GRU-based iterative unit progressively predicts residual depth and finally regresses the complete depth map.",
      "page": 3,
      "captionRect": [
        58.5,
        206.5041046142578,
        553.4990844726562,
