  {
    "id": "cvpr26-e65aa1c25c0c",
    "extraction": {
      "figure": "Figure 1",
      "caption": "Figure 1 : Overall framework of HiCoDiT . We formulate video-to-speech generation as a hierarchical masked token prediction task. Speech is tokenized using an RVQ codec and split into low-level components 𝒙 r 1 : r 2 t \\bm{x}^{r_{1}:r_{2}}_{t} and high-level components 𝒙 r 3 : r 12 t \\bm{x}^{r_{3}:r_{12}}_{t} , reflecting the intrinsic hierarchy of speech tokens. Guided by this structure, we disentangle visual features from the input video 𝒱 \\mathcal{V} into lip motion 𝒄 lip \\bm{c}_{\\text{lip}} , identity 𝒄 id \\bm{c}_{\\text{id}} , and emotion 𝒄 emo \\bm{c}_{\\text{emo}} , and inject them into the corresponding diffusion blocks. Finally, score heads take output features 𝒉 t low \\bm{h}_{t}^{\\text{low}} and 𝒉 t high \\bm{h}_{t}^{\\text{high}} from both blocks to predict concrete scores of all level tokens for unmasking.",
      "image_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2604.15923v1/main.png",
      "figureAnchor": "S4.F1",
      "panelIndex": 0,
      "panelCount": 1,
      "score": 26,
