    "extraction": {
      "figure": "Figure 2",
      "caption": "Figure 2 : Architecture of the proposed framework. It integrates three modules (JSRL, VGII, and AFRI) to form a closed-loop pipeline of encoding, inference, fusion, and reconstruction. JSRL learns a shared dictionary for cross-modal alignment, VGII predicts latent infrared coefficients from visible ones, and AFRI fuses both modalities in the coefficient domain to reconstruct consistent, high-quality images under missing-IR conditions.",
      "image_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2603.08018v2/Fig2.png",
      "figureAnchor": "S1.F2",
