    "id": "cvpr26-c302d6fdc731",
    "extraction": {
      "figure": "Figure 2",
      "caption": "Figure 2 : Pipeline overview. From a surface 𝒮 \\mathcal{S} , we sample points and geometric features (normals, local features).\nAround an ε \\varepsilon - narrow band around the shape, we gather Cartesian grids ℬ 𝒮 \\mathcal{B}_{\\mathcal{S}} to store an initial field U 0 U_{0} extended from surface values and covered by overlapping, surface-centred patches { 𝒫 i } \\{\\mathcal{P}_{i}\\} .\nEach patch is reoriented to its local frame, yielding { ℬ ^ i , ℱ ^ i } \\{\\hat{\\mathcal{B}}_{i},\\hat{\\mathcal{F}}_{i}\\} , which are processed by our lightweight geometry-conditioned operators 𝒩 Θ \\mathcal{N}_{\\Theta} to produce local updates (see Figure 3 ).\nThe local updates are smoothly aggregated to form the global band update U ~ t \\tilde{U}_{t} and advanced with a standard grid PDE time step to get U t + 1 U_{t+1} .\nIterating this loop yields surface PDE solutions directly in the neural domain via grid-to-grid updates, without mesh extraction or extend–restrict shuttling.",
      "image_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2512.21311v2/neuralPDE_pipeline.png",
      "figureAnchor": "S3.F2",
      "panelIndex": 0,
      "panelCount": 1,
